---
import SectionIntro from "@/components/SectionIntro.astro";
---

<section class="section-pad">
  <div class="shell">
    <SectionIntro
      index="05"
      label="AI"
      title="Practical use, not hype."
      description="Production software, not demos that never ship."
    />

    <p class="prose-block max-w-2xl">
      I use AI where it solves a clear problem: saving time, improving a workflow,
      or making data easier to use.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-10 grid max-w-3xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Integration.</span>
        GPT, Claude, LLama, and other models in existing products with sensible
        guardrails.
      </li>
      <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Automation.</span>
        Document handling, data extraction, internal support workflows.
      </li>
      <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Knowledge.</span>
        Search over your own data with RAG and vector storage where needed.
      </li>
      <li class="text-base leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Strategy.</span>
        Working out where AI is worth the effort, and where it is not.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="prose-block mt-8 max-w-2xl font-mono text-xs text-text-muted">
      OpenAI · Claude · LangChain · vector DBs · RAG · fine-tuning · prompt
      engineering
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
